# Drafted by Gemini (R18 hook), edited.

~ rain_start
Narrator: Sister Rain steps beneath the pavilion lanterns with damp soil on her hem and a tremor in her fingers. The smell of cold turnip broth hangs between you.
sister_rain [afraid]: Forgive me for coming late to the table, friends, but the commune north of Moonsong Lake is failing. Their orchards, their cattle, and their folk are rotting where they stand.
sister_rain [weary]: While I laid cool cloths on the fevered this morning, a waking vision struck me blind. Please, someone steady has to walk into those woods before nothing remains.
* What did you see? -> vision
* Tell us about the commune. -> commune
* We will go. -> accept
* Not yet. -> refuse

~ vision
sister_rain [afraid]: I saw a canopy of wet emerald timber stretching out under the moon, and every trunk was crowded with watching faces. Mouths full of moss, weeping and waiting for us.
-> rain_start

~ commune
sister_rain [sad]: They are quiet Patient Lady folk who built a longhouse and planted apple trees by the water. They sent one runner begging for medicine, and then the road went silent.
sister_rain [angry]: You can feel the land aching right through the soles of your boots if you stand still enough. Something up there is eating the green out of the world.
-> rain_start

~ accept
sister_rain [smile]: Bless your boots and your blades, truly. Take these bottles of Harvest Brew for the road, and do not drink the forest water once the moss turns pale.
give harvest_brew 4
set hb_asked
set hb_rain_hook_accepted
if not quest.q_hartsblight >= hook
quest q_hartsblight hook
endif
Narrator: Outside the palisade, a carpet of green-white spores glows faintly in the wheel ruts, pointing north-west toward the lake. It looks to be four nights on foot.
-> END

~ refuse
sister_rain [sad]: I cannot force your steps onto a dark road, and the Lady knows you carry enough already. Pray the wind stays in the south tonight.
set hb_refused = now
-> END

~ rain_again
sister_rain [weary]: I promised myself I would not beg twice over the same cold supper, so I will speak plainly. The sickness north of the lake is not waiting on our courage.
* We will go now. -> accept
* Still no. -> END

~ wendel_offer
cutscene hb_sporefall
Narrator: For eight quiet hours before dawn, pale green dust sifts down from the crone's moon like greasy snow, coating every roof and rain barrel in Wickermoor Hollow.
cutscene hb_sporefall_2
cutscene end
wendel_somerton [afraid]: Lock the casement behind you, I beg you, before more of that dreadful powder drifts onto the carpet. The wells taste of cellar mould and the whole parish is panicking.
wendel_somerton [weary]: The Old Ways elders are holding emergency rituals in the lanes, and folks are whispering of famine. I will pay three hundred gold pieces to each of you to end this.
* We will end it. -> wendel_accept
* What are the rituals? -> wendel_rituals
* Not yet. -> END

~ wendel_rituals
wendel_somerton [neutral]: Little wicker stag effigies burned at the crossroads to turn the rot aside, all properly licensed and modest in size. My clerk issued the permits before his throat swelled shut.
-> wendel_offer

~ wendel_accept
wendel_somerton [smile]: Splendid, truly a weight off the municipal ledger and my own poor chest. Sister Rain left these cordials on my porch for you before she went back to the infirmary.
give harvest_brew 4
set hb_asked
set hb_sporefall
if not quest.q_hartsblight >= hook
quest q_hartsblight hook
endif
Narrator: The spore trail lies thick as lamb's wool along the north-west cart track, smelling faintly of bruised apples and wet bone.
-> END
